It would make me shaky knowing that a minoraur is on such a shallow level
and alive, I'd prefer to kill him *if* I can as early as possible. But
the minotaur has speed 15, i.e. he is faster than the normal speed of 12,
and melee contact might kill you even in one turn (3d10, 3d10, 2d8). So
that completely rules out melee. But as a ranger you can kill him from
distance. An option might be to have him in a (preferably long) corridor,
and a boulder between you and that beast; then you may shoot missiles.
An additional option is to immobilize him with a sleep ray. But, again,
don't be cocky and melee the sleeping beauty but kill him from distance.
It may be worth to leave and first train your bow skill to become expert
(in case you aren't yet), then come back to kill him. One option that is
inspired by the ranger's quest; you can get a bear trap (you'll even
find one in the quest[*]) to immobilize the one you are concerned of by
activating it in your current dungeon level at some appropriate place.
If you don't have any means to perform such a secure procedure, leave
the level and don't forget that he's still there when you're coming back.

